Dynamic Link モジュールのサンプルコードを示します。 Dynamic Link モジュールはShadow オブジェクトの'script' に設定され、dlopen() によってPD Agent for AWS IoT に取り込まれます。 Dynamic Link モジュールには、dl init(), dl main(), dl fini() の三つの関数を定義することができます。 dl init() は起動時に、dl main() はメッセージが出力される都度(UNIX ドメインソケットへ出力 する直前)、dl fini() は停止時に、呼び出されます。 dl main() の引数には、Thing name と Shadow name が 'const char ' で、'desired', 'reported', 'delta' の各オブジェクトが jansson C library の 'json t ' で与えられます。 'void context' は、dl init() で定義され dl main(), dl fini() に継承することのできるコンテキストです。戻り値には 'update' メッセージでDevice Shadow に送る 'reported' オブジェクトを 'json t ' で与えます。 戻り値が NULL の場合はエラーとして扱われるため、Shadow オブジェクトの'behalf' をtrue に設定している場合でも空のオブジェクトなどのダミーを返す必要があります。 本サンプルコードは、/usr/share/pdhms/agent＿awsiot/dl_module_skelton.c としてインストールされています。 dl_module_skelton.c# /* * Copyright (c) 2021 * Plat'Home CO., LTD. <support@plathome.co.jp>. All rights reserved. * * Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without * modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions * are met: * 1. Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright * notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer. * 2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright * notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in the * documentation and/or other materials provided with the distribution. * 3. Neither the name of the Plat'Home CO., LTD. nor the names of * its contributors may be used to endorse or promote products derived * from this software without specific prior written permission. * * THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED BY THE AUTHOR ``AS IS'' AND ANY EXPRESS OR * IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, THE IMPLIED * WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE * ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, * INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES * (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR * SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS; OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) * HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT * LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY * OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF * SUCH DAMAGE. */ #include <stdio.h> #include <time.h> #include <jansson.h> /* Your own initialize function : int dl_init() It is called only once at startup. void **context : pointer for context. Return value : 0 for normal. -1 for error. */ int dl_init(void **context) { return(0); } /* Your own finalize function : int dl_fini() It is called only once at termination. void *context : pointer for context. Return value : none. */ void dl_fini(void *context) { return; } /* Your own exec function : dl_main() void *context : pointer for context. const char *thingName : Thing name for Device Shadow. const char *shadowName : Shadow name for Device Shadow. json_t *desired : desired JSON object for the current Device Shadow. json_t *reported : reported JSON object for the Device Shadow. json_t *delta : delta JSON object for the Device Shadow. Return value : JSON object (json_t *) to be report by update. NULL for error. */ json_t *dl_main(void *context, const char *thingName, const char *shadowName, json_t *desired, json_t *reported, json_t *delta) { FILE *fp; json_t *obj; time_t current; if (!(fp = fopen("/tmp/my_func1.txt", "a"))) { return((json_t *)NULL); } fprintf(fp, "%s/%s
", thingName, shadowName); obj = json_object(); time(&current); json_object_set(obj, "desired", desired); json_object_set(obj, "reported", reported); json_object_set(obj, "delte", delta); json_object_set(obj, "timestamp", json_integer(current)); fprintf(fp, "%s

", json_dumps(obj, JSON_INDENT(4))); fclose(fp); json_decref(obj); json_object_update(reported, delta); return(reported); }

